DDIIAAGGNNOOSSTTIICCSS
     ccppddiirr prints a usage message and exits 1 if given a bad
     option or not exactly two directory arguments.  During the
     copy, it reports (and, without -ee, stops on) conditions such
     as a source or target that cannot be found, opened, or read;
     a target that is not a directory or lacks needed permission;
     a device boundary crossing; a link that could not be
     recreated; or running out of memory.  With -ee, ccppddiirr exits 1
     at the end if any error occurred.
